  "title": "Concept-Driven Domain Adaptation and Continual Personalization Frameworks",
  "summary": "Concept-Driven Domain Adaptation (CDDA) and Continual Low-rank Adapters (CLASP) address the challenges of adapting vision-language models to concept-level retrieval. CDDA proposes a staged framework for concept-aware geometry transfer, while CLASP leverages a single hypernetwork for continuous personalization, preserving learned concepts and enabling spatial control without additional parameters.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "CDDA treats concepts as intermediate semantic anchors in vision-language models for concept-level adaptation.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "CLASP dynamically produces concept-specific adaptations for continuous personalization using a fixed-size hypernetwork.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both frameworks achieve strong pedagogical success while maintaining parameter efficiency for long-term personalization tasks.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
